{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/432150-flesh-eating-and-major-templates","id":432150,"title":"Flesh Eating and Major Templates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-07T19:48:59-08:00","id":432150,"title":"Flesh Eating and Major Templates","content":"Do werewolves gain essence from eating Mages, Vampires, Changelings and such?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T19:57:18-08:00","id":432171,"title":"","content":"Very likely that they get essence from Changelings and Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T20:17:41-08:00","id":432176,"title":"","content":"I would say Mages are physically human, so they count.<br /> <br /> Vampires are the corpses of humans that happen to be walking under their own power, so I would say they're perfectly edible as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T20:19:24-08:00","id":432177,"title":"","content":"From Mages: Yes.<br /> From Demons: In Cover, yes.<br /> From Mummies: Without Ammut's blessing, ain't nothing eating the Arisen/Deceived.<br /> From Sin Eaters:Yes, and it might even count as being Essence rich.<br /> From Changelings: THe eight ball's fuzzy on that one, I'm leaning toward no.<br /> Prommies: Probably not.<br /> Vampires: Hazy, but probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T20:23:39-08:00","id":432178,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I was looking for ways werewolves could deal agg damage to non-werewolves. The only reference I found that wasn't against spirits or other werewolves was flesh-eating. This might be something good to get into the FAQ when one is made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T20:25:45-08:00","id":432179,"title":"","content":"There won't be much of an &quot;official&quot; answer on this, or at least the edge cases, so you'll have to draw your own rulings for your games.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm inclined to say that werewolves who devour living and/or mostly human beings gain Essence. This means mages, changelings, Sin-Eaters for sure. Demons, at least those in Cover? Yes, though I might say that they're not worth as much, since it's like eating soup that is mostly water. There's nutrition there, but a lot of stuff of no value to you. Prometheans and vampires definitely not. They're not alive in the same way as the other things are, and in the case of Prometheans were never human at all.<br /> <br /> Note that this is just one freelancer's personal thoughts on it, and in no way represents an official ruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T20:29:20-08:00","id":432181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/432150-flesh-eating-and-major-templates?p=432179#post432179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There won't be much of an &quot;official&quot; answer on this, or at least the edge cases, so you'll have to draw your own rulings for your games.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm inclined to say that werewolves who devour living and/or mostly human beings gain Essence. This means mages, changelings, Sin-Eaters for sure. Demons, at least those in Cover? Yes, though I might say that they're not worth as much, since it's like eating soup that is mostly water. There's nutrition there, but a lot of stuff of no value to you. Prometheans and vampires definitely not. They're not alive in the same way as the other things are, and in the case of Prometheans were never human at all.<br /> <br /> Note that this is just one freelancer's personal thoughts on it, and in no way represents an official ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense-Vampire provided a merit that just made it easy, might as well keep it simple for other questions along those lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T20:33:14-08:00","id":432201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container 